    <div class="page">
        <p>The amount on line 3-$7,500 is less than the amount on line 6-$10,925. Subtracting $10,925 from $7,500 pro-duces a negative amount. As a result, Riley and Parker may not claim the credit.</p>
        <div class="section-title">How To Get Tax Help</div>
        <p>If you have questions about a tax issue, need help prep-aring your tax return, or want to download free publications, go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov" data-field="irs_website">{{ irs_website }}</a> to find resources that can help you right away.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Preparing and filing your tax return.</div>
        <p>After receiving all your wage and earnings statements (Forms W-2, W-2G, 1099-INT, 1099-MISC, etc.), unemployment compensation statements (vital or in a digital format) or other government payment statements (Form 1099-G) and interest, dividend, and retirement statements from banks and investment firms (Forms 1099), you have sev-eral options for preparing and filing your tax retur-n. You can prepare the tax return yourself, see if you qualify for free tax preparation, or hire a tax professional to prepare your return.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Free options for tax preparation.</div>
        <p>Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov" data-field="irs_free_prep_link">{{ irs_free_prep_link }}</a> to see your options for preparing and filing your return online in your local community. If you qualify, which include the fol-lowing:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Free File.</strong> This program lets you prepare and file your federal individual income tax return for free using brand-name tax preparation and filing software or free file publications. However, state tax preparation is not offered through Free File. Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov" data-field="irs_free_file_link">{{ irs_free_file_link }}</a> for Free File to see if you qualify for free online federal tax preparation.</li>
            <li><strong>VITA.</strong> The Volunteer Income Tax Assistance (VITA) program offers free tax help to people with low-to-moderate incomes, persons with disabilities, limited English-speaking taxpayers, and taxpayers who need help preparing their own tax returns. Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov" data-field="irs_vita_link">{{ irs_vita_link }}</a> for VITA, download the free IRS2Go app, or call 800-900-3683 for information on free tax return prepa-ration.</li>
            <li><strong>TEC.</strong> The Tax Counseling for the Elderly (TCE) pro-gram offers free tax help for all taxpayers, particularly those who are 60 years of age and older. TCE volun-teers specialize in answering questions about pen-sions and retirement-related tax issues unique to seniors. Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov" data-field="irs_tce_link">{{ irs_tce_link }}</a>, download the free IRS2Go app, or call 888-227-7669 for information on free tax return preparation.</li>
            <li><strong>MIFTax.</strong> Members of the U.S. Armed Forces and quali-fied veterans may use MIFTax, a free tax service of-fered by the Department of Defense through Military OneSource. For more information, go to <a href="https://www.militaryonesource.mil/miftax" data-field="military_onesource_link">{{ military_onesource_link }}</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="page">
        <p><strong>Publication 524 (2023)</strong></p>
        <div class="section-title">Getting answers to your tax questions.</div>
        <p>On <a href="https://www.irs.gov" data-field="irs_website_link">{{ irs_website_link }}</a>, you can get up-to-date information on current events and changes in tax law.</p>
        <p><strong>The Earned Income Tax Credit Assistant (IRS.gov/EITCassistant)</strong> determines if you're eligible for the earned income credit (EIC).</p>
        <p><strong>The Online EIN Application (IRS.gov/EIN)</strong> helps you get an employer identification number (EIN) at no cost.</p>
        <div class="section-title">The Tax Withholding Estimator (IRS.gov/W4app)</div>
        <p>This tool helps you estimate the federal income tax you want your employer to withhold from your paychecks. Check this tool to see how your withhold-ing affects your federal, state, and local tax.</p>
        <div class="section-title">The First-Time Homebuyer Credit Lookup on IRS.gov</div>
        <p>This tool provides information on your requirements and account balance.</p>
        <div class="section-title">The Sales Tax Deduction Calculator (IRS.gov/SalesTax)</div>
        <p>This tool figures out how much you can claim if you itemize deductions on Schedule A (Form 1040).</p>
        <div class="section-title">Filing an amended return.</div>
        <p>Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov/form1040x" data-field="form1040x_link">{{ form1040x_link }}</a> for information and updates.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Checking the status of your amended return.</div>
        <p>Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov/amendedreturns" data-field="amended_return_status_link">{{ amended_return_status_link }}</a> to track the status of Form 1040-X amend-ed returns.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Understanding an IRS notice or letter you've re-ceived.</div>
        <p>Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov/notices" data-field="irs_notices_link">{{ irs_notices_link }}</a> to find additional informa-tion about responding to an IRS notice or letter.</p>
        <p>Note. You can use Schedule LEP (Form 1040), Re-quest for Change in Language Preference, to state a pref-erence to receive notices, letters, or other written commu-nications from the IRS in an alternative language. You may also receive communications in a language other than English if you are part of a multi-year timeline that is scheduled to be de-livered in a language other than English.</p>
        <p><strong>Publication 524 (2023)</strong></p>
        <p><strong>Page 10</strong></p>
    </div>
    <div class="page">
        <p>more information on how to choose a tax preparer, go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov" data-field="irs_tax_preparer_link">{{ irs_tax_preparer_link }}</a>.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Coronavirus.</div>
        <p>Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov/coronavirus" data-field="irs_coronavirus_link">{{ irs_coronavirus_link }}</a> for links to in-formation on the impact of the coronavirus, as well as tax relief available for individuals and families, small and large businesses, and tax-exempt organizations.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Employers can register to use Business Services On-line.</div>
        <p>The Social Security Administration (SSA) offers on-line service at <a href="https://www.ssa.gov/employer" data-field="ssa_employer_link">{{ ssa_employer_link }}</a> for free, secure on-line filing of W-2s, wage and tax statements, and other wage and tax statements. For more information, see the SSA website.</p>
        <div class="section-title">IRS social media.</div>
        <p>Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov/socialmedia" data-field="irs_social_media_link">{{ irs_social_media_link }}</a> to see the various social media tools the IRS uses to share the latest information on tax changes, scams, alerts, initiatives, prod-ucts, and more. The IRS uses these tools to share its highest priority. We use these tools to share public information, not to give tax advice. Always protect your social security number and other confidential information on social media sites. Always protect your identity when using any social media site.</p>
        <p>When using IRS YouTube channels provide short, in-format videos on various tax-related topics in English, Spanish, and ASL.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/c/IRS" data-field="irs_youtube_link">{{ irs_youtube_link }}</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/c/IRSvideos" data-field="irs_videos_link">{{ irs_videos_link }}</a></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="section-title">Watching IRS videos.</div>
        <p>The IRS Video portal (<a href="https://www.irs.gov/videos" data-field="irs_videos_portal_link">{{ irs_videos_portal_link }}</a>) contains video and audio presentations for individuals, small businesses, and tax professionals.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Online tax information in other languages.</div>
        <p>You can find information on <a href="https://www.irs.gov/my/language" data-field="irs_language_link">{{ irs_language_link }}</a> if English isn't your native language.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Free Over-the-Phone Interpreter (OPI) Service.</div>
        <p>The IRS is committed to serving our multilingual customers by offering OPI services. The OPI Service is a federally fun-ded program and is available at Taxpayer Assistance Cen-ters (TACS), other IRS offices, and every VITA/TCE center site. The OPI Service is accessible in more than 350 lan-guages.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Accessibility Helpline available for taxpayers with disabilities.</div>
        <p>Taxpayers who need information for people with disabilities. Taxpayers who need information for people with disabilities can call 800-900-0599. The Accessi-lity Helpline can answer questions related to current and future accessibility products and services available in al-ternative media formats (for example, braille, large print, audio, etc.). The Accessibility Helpline does not have ac-cess to your IRS account. For help with tax law, refunds, or account-related issues, go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov/help" data-field="irs_help_link">{{ irs_help_link }}</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="page">
        <div class="section-title">Tax Pro Account.</div>
        <p>This tool lets your tax professional submit an authorization request to access your individual taxpayer <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxproaccount" data-field="taxproaccount_link">{{ taxproaccount_link }}</a>. For more information, go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxproaccount" data-field="irs_taxproaccount_info_link">{{ irs_taxproaccount_info_link }}</a>.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Using direct deposit.</div>
        <p>The fastest way to receive a tax refund is to file electronically and choose direct deposit, which securely and electronically transfers your refund di-rectly into your financial account. Direct deposit also avoids the possibility that your check could be lost, stolen, destroyed, or returned undeliverable to the IRS. Eight in</p>
        <div class="section-title">How Else Does TAS Help Taxpayers?</div>
        <p>TAS works to resolve large-scale problems that affect many taxpayers. If you know of one of these broad issues, report it to them at <a href="https://www.irs.gov/tas" data-field="irs_tas_link">{{ irs_tas_link }}</a>.</p>
